  "aiContextParagraph": "President Donald Trump has appointed Stephen Miller to serve as the new White House chief of staff. Miller, aged 41, assumed the role on Monday, replacing Susie Wiles. His appointment follows the recent midterm election cycle, which resulted in a defeat for the Republican party. Miller is widely recognized for his involvement in shaping the administration's immigration policies, including mass deportation initiatives. Current reports suggest that federal agencies, such as Immigration and Customs Enforcement, are not expected to scale back their enforcement activities under his leadership. Meanwhile, the political atmosphere in Congress remains complex, with some lawmakers expressing hesitation regarding future legislative cooperation given Miller's past policy positions. The appointment has garnered significant international attention as the administration prepares for upcoming legislative challenges and continues to emphasize its core policy agenda.",
